research/audit/wave7-proof-contracts.json-21896-        "notes": "critical risk (13): 12 declared dependencies; 13 cited facts; 7 numbered proof steps; biconditional / both-direction claim; boundary-sensitive language; analytic limiting/completeness language, routed by risk-report.mjs. The read-only DeepSeek V4 Pro audit-refuter received the complete target and every cited dependency and returned CLEAN. Boundary evidence: The domain is $p \\in \\mathbb{Q}$, $p>0$; the boundary $p=1$ (ratio $1$, divergence) and the endpoints $p=1/2$ and $p=2$ are checked directly and agree with the claimed threshold. The zero case $p=0$ is excluded by hypothesis, and $k=0$ is excluded because $1/0^p$ is undefined; no other degenerate or empty cases arise. The equivalence chain $\\sum 1/k^p$ converges $\\iff$ condensed series converges $\\iff$ $2^{1-p}<1$ $\\iff$ $p>1$ is valid for all admitted $p$, and no counterexample was found. Checked surface: The title, the public claim in the Example section, every numbered verification step (1.1–4.1), and the Remarks were read. No mathematical defect, missing hypothesis, or invalid inference was found. Alpha adjudicated the return against the current item and cited dependencies on disk and found no fatal mathematical or dependency-citation defect. Evidence: research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/ex-condensation-applied--80b568a248a6d796.result.json."
