research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-evt-and-ivt-fail-over-a-non-complete-field.md-178-      "fact": "L1",
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-evt-and-ivt-fail-over-a-non-complete-field.md-179-      "source": "def-field",
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-evt-and-ivt-fail-over-a-non-complete-field.md-180-      "source_section": "Definition",
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-evt-and-ivt-fail-over-a-non-complete-field.md:181:      "quote": "A **field** is a set $F$ equipped with two binary operations $+$ (addition) and\n$\\cdot$ (multiplication) and two distinguished elements $0 \\ne 1$ of $F$,\nsatisfying:\n\n- **(A)** $(F, +)$ is an abelian group with identity $0$: addition is\n  associative and commutative, $x + 0 = x$ for all $x$, and every $x$ has an\n  additive inverse $-x$ with $x + (-x) = 0$.\n- **(M)** Multiplication is associative and commutative **on all of $F$**, and\n  $x \\cdot 1 = x$ for every $x \\in F$; moreover $(F \\setminus \\{0\\}, \\cdot)$ is an\n  abelian group with identity $1$, so every $x \\ne 0$ has a multiplicative inverse\n  $x^{-1}$ with $x \\cdot x^{-1} = 1$.\n- **(D)** Multiplication distributes over addition: $x \\cdot (y + z) = x\\cdot y + x\\cdot z$.\n\nWe write $x - y := x + (-y)$ and $x/y := x \\cdot y^{-1}$ (for $y \\ne 0$), and\nabbreviate $x \\cdot y$ as $xy$.",
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-evt-and-ivt-fail-over-a-non-complete-field.md-182-      "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-evt-and-ivt-fail-over-a-non-complete-field.md-183-        "1.2",
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-evt-and-ivt-fail-over-a-non-complete-field.md-184-        "3.1"
--
