items/rem-homology-and-cohomology.md-30-## Statement
items/rem-homology-and-cohomology.md-31-
items/rem-homology-and-cohomology.md:32:**Singular homology.** To each topological space $X$ one associates abelian
items/rem-homology-and-cohomology.md-33-groups $H_k(X)$, $k \geq 0$, as the homology of the chain complex whose $k$-chains
items/rem-homology-and-cohomology.md-34-are formal integer combinations of continuous maps $\Delta^k \to X$. The
items/rem-homology-and-cohomology.md-35-construction is functorial, and the properties that make it usable are:
--
items/rem-homology-and-cohomology.md-43-* the **Eilenberg-Steenrod axioms**, which characterise the theory uniquely on CW
items/rem-homology-and-cohomology.md-44-  pairs once the value on a point is fixed.
