research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-abel-dini--2ec0d3834efb2fd5.prompt.md-1409-
research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-abel-dini--2ec0d3834efb2fd5.prompt.md-1410-[L1] For a series of nonnegative terms: the partial sums are nondecreasing, and if the series diverges their range is not bounded above and they diverge to $+\infty$ ([[thm-nonnegative-series-bounded-partial-sums]], [[lem-monotone-unbounded-diverges]], [[def-monotone-sequence]], [[def-divergence-to-infinity]]).
research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-abel-dini--2ec0d3834efb2fd5.prompt.md-1411-
research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-abel-dini--2ec0d3834efb2fd5.prompt.md:1412:[L2] Abel-Dini: if $(a_k)$ has positive terms and $\sum a_k$ diverges, then with $S_n = \sum_{k=0}^{n} a_k$ the series $\sum_n a_n/S_n$ diverges ([[thm-abel-dini]]).
research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-abel-dini--2ec0d3834efb2fd5.prompt.md-1413-
research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/thm-abel-dini--2ec0d3834efb2fd5.prompt.md-1414-[L3] Order and reciprocals: for $x > 0$ and $y > 1$ one has $0 < x/y < x$ ([[lem-of-inverse-positive]]); and a sum of positive terms is positive ([[lem-finite-sum-laws]]).
