items/lem-linear-subspace-is-a-subgroup.md-53-
items/lem-linear-subspace-is-a-subgroup.md-54-**Given:** A field $F$, a vector space $V$ over $F$, and a subset $W \subseteq V$.
items/lem-linear-subspace-is-a-subgroup.md-55-
items/lem-linear-subspace-is-a-subgroup.md:56:[L1] Axiom (V1): $(V,+,0_V)$ is an abelian group ([[def-vector-space]], [[def-group]]).
items/lem-linear-subspace-is-a-subgroup.md-57-
items/lem-linear-subspace-is-a-subgroup.md-58-[L2] A subgroup of a group $G$ with identity $e$ is a subset $H$ satisfying (S1) $e \in H$, (S2) $x, y \in H$ implies $xy \in H$, and (S3) $x \in H$ implies $x^{-1} \in H$; such an $H$, with the restricted operation, is itself a group whose identity and whose inverses are those of $G$ ([[def-subgroup]]).
items/lem-linear-subspace-is-a-subgroup.md-59-
