items/def-local-path-packings-and-separators.md-54-$S\subseteq V\setminus\{s,t\}$ for which deleting $S$, together with every
items/def-local-path-packings-and-separators.md:55:incident arc or edge label, leaves no $s$-$t$ path occurrence. The local vertex
items/def-local-path-packings-and-separators.md-56-comparison is used only when the terminals are nonadjacent (or, in the directed
items/def-local-path-packings-and-separators.md:57:case, when no arc label has tail $s$ and head $t$), so that such a separator can
items/def-local-path-packings-and-separators.md-58-exist.
