items/lem-ring-elementary-consequences.md-48-
items/lem-ring-elementary-consequences.md-49-**Given:** A ring $R$ with zero $0$, identity $1$, addition $+$ and multiplication $\cdot$, and elements $a, b, c \in R$; $x - y$ abbreviates $x + (-y)$ ([[def-ring]]).
items/lem-ring-elementary-consequences.md-50-
items/lem-ring-elementary-consequences.md:51:[L1] $(R,+,0)$ is an abelian group: addition is associative and commutative, $0 + x = x = x + 0$, and each $x$ has an additive inverse $-x$ with $x + (-x) = 0 = (-x) + x$ ([[def-ring]], [[def-group]], [[def-identity-element]]).
items/lem-ring-elementary-consequences.md-52-
items/lem-ring-elementary-consequences.md-53-[L2] Both distributive laws hold: $x(y+z) = xy + xz$ and $(y+z)x = yx + zx$ for all $x, y, z \in R$ ([[def-ring]]).
