items/lem-abel-transform-of-cesaro-means.md:21:Let $S_n:=\sum_{k=0}^{n}a_k$ and $\sigma_n:=\iota(n+1)^{-1}\sum_{k=0}^{n}S_k$. If $(\sigma_n)$ is bounded, then for every $0<x<1$ the Abel series converges and
items/lem-abel-transform-of-cesaro-means.md-22-
items/lem-abel-transform-of-cesaro-means.md-23-$$\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}a_nx^n=(1-x)^2\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\iota(n+1)\sigma_nx^n.$$
