items/thm-principal-inverse-tangent-calculus.md:72:4.1 Let $S:=\sum_{n\ge0}(-1)^n/(2n+1)$, which exists by [L6].  Abel's theorem and step 3.1 yield $$S=\lim_{x\uparrow1}\sum_{n\ge0}\frac{(-1)^nx^{2n+1}}{2n+1} =\lim_{x\uparrow1}\arctan x=\arctan1.$$ By [L7] and the principal range, $\arctan1=\pi/4$.  [step 3.1, L1, L6, L7]
