items/thm-quaternions-form-a-division-ring.md-69-[L4] Finite sums in the commutative monoid $(\mathbb{R},+,0)$ are defined by [[def-monoid-finite-product]] read additively, and their value is unchanged by regrouping the summands or permuting them ([[thm-generalised-associativity]], [[def-semigroup-and-monoid]], [[def-binary-operation]]).
items/thm-quaternions-form-a-division-ring.md-70-
items/thm-quaternions-form-a-division-ring.md:71:[L5] A ring is an abelian group under addition, a monoid under multiplication, and satisfies both distributive laws; a division ring is a ring with $1 \ne 0$ in which every nonzero element is a unit; the units of a ring form a group ([[def-ring]], [[def-division-ring]], [[def-invertible-element]], [[lem-ring-units-form-a-group]]).
items/thm-quaternions-form-a-division-ring.md-72-
items/thm-quaternions-form-a-division-ring.md-73-[L6] Every field is a commutative ring ([[lem-field-is-a-commutative-ring]]).
