items/ex-integers-mod-n-additive-group.md:72:[L5] A group is a monoid all of whose elements are invertible; abelian means commutative; the order $|G|$ of a finite group is the unique natural $m$ with $G \approx m$; $\langle g \rangle$ is the smallest subgroup containing $g$ and equals the set of integer powers of $g$ ([[def-group]], [[def-binary-operation]], [[def-identity-element]], [[def-order-in-a-group]], [[def-generated-subgroup]], [[lem-cyclic-subgroup-is-the-set-of-powers]], [[def-countable]], [[def-equinumerous]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
