items/lem-cyclic-subgroup-is-the-set-of-powers.md:78:4.1 Any two elements of $P$ commute: $g^{m} g^{n} = g^{n} g^{m}$ for all integers $m, n$. Hence $\langle g \rangle$ is abelian, by step 3.1. [step 3.1, L2]
