items/ex-additive-and-multiplicative-groups-of-a-field.md-66-1.2 $0$ is a two-sided identity for $+$: $x + 0 = x$ by (A), and $0 + x = x + 0 = x$ by commutativity. So $(F,+,0)$ is a commutative monoid. [L1, L4]
