items/ex-additive-and-multiplicative-groups-of-a-field.md-76-4.1 Every $x \in F \setminus \{0\}$ is invertible there: (M) supplies $x^{-1} \in F$ with $x x^{-1} = 1$, and $x^{-1} \ne 0$ since otherwise $1 = x \cdot 0 = 0$, contradicting $0 \ne 1$; commutativity gives $x^{-1} x = 1$ as well, so $x^{-1}$ is a two-sided inverse lying in $F \setminus \{0\}$. [step 1.4, step 3.1, L2, L3]
items/ex-additive-and-multiplicative-groups-of-a-field.md-77-
