research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-4-{"id":"ex-r-and-open-interval-homeomorphic-not-uniformly-isomorphic","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"L3 inaccurately says the cited corollary states that 1/n converges to 0. Its statement only gives, for each positive epsilon, one natural n with 1/n below epsilon; the eventual convergence form is only discussed in remarks and requires an additional monotonicity argument.","context_sha256":"4eb1c073711dcf7b660bf2ab1e32253b3277dbd4fddfacc2fb1e6d47238918e6","item_sha256":"91633459c3025ae67675a7a2faf4d1e4b80ea3b1dcb080f112113ca73c6af767","at":"2026-08-08T19:12:32.652Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-5-{"id":"def-uniform-cover-space","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"The final sentence mis-cites lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary: that lemma proves equivalence with entourage uniformities, but neither its statement nor proof proves that a uniform-cover structure induces a topology.","context_sha256":"9f1a0a47f935562dfa506ab879173c751ec5216ac13b13e058e58f3620ee6a3b","item_sha256":"64c44142057a572ab6a5dfba95bb41f44f94d7ca53933c9cfeb4007a703b9b07","at":"2026-08-08T19:12:32.655Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-6-{"id":"cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified both implications: the cited facts faithfully supply complete regularity, Hausdorffness, singleton closure, and the separating gauge.","context_sha256":"723734b8920f593979ac8a95d973c4d7d03dba292fef6ea28de6c52c4692cdf0","item_sha256":"b5bb5a54d052cd72cbf1aeb4835516546d0e7ddb36c187a4b161772f51d939f0","at":"2026-08-08T19:12:35.717Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-7-{"id":"ex-sierpinski-space-is-normal-and-not-completely-regular","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the cited refutation establishes normality and failure of complete regularity, and the closed-set calculation correctly shows failure of T1.","context_sha256":"0327c06a8e9af8d20e27f1194bbbaa488d313a204538bb8130e1de62b7bfb4a4","item_sha256":"83459a9450f10ef1566347b4bc230d4f95f94c0a0359cedf7cfb1b73c4cd51cf","at":"2026-08-08T19:12:38.778Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-8-{"id":"def-gauge-of-pseudometrics","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the finite simultaneous balls form a proper directed base on nonempty X; pseudometric symmetry and triangle inequality give the uniformity axioms, and each gauge member has its balls in it.","context_sha256":"c10e9323395214d6508cdb73daf19a2cd4382f1d0f4d22c208c8a1b621041469","item_sha256":"3e786bab30b61294ab7f87c86a3e0458e6e767b2ed7fed340edabeb9e85e1a22","at":"2026-08-08T19:12:41.264Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl:9:{"id":"ex-harmonic-series-diverges","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"The introduction falsely calls harmonic divergence the slowest exhibited on the page. The Abel-Dini sibling explicitly gives the divergent series 1/(k H_k) and states that it diverges more slowly still.","context_sha256":"0153498dd3e71524d06e01e588223f1d43294cb2875b60c627fc75efa4163788","item_sha256":"dfaa02b7731703fcb77aeb621a75b2d99e1a764376dff1335f9f9eecb42d6e9d","at":"2026-08-08T19:12:48.683Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-10-{"id":"cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the compact-cover argument and its cited uniform-cover dictionary correctly supply one source entourage controlling the target entourage.","context_sha256":"72051c01ca787f8cc59591f1c85b05798910db26d85be106b63ca28513c79f18","item_sha256":"ac90070ff2390643ceb4bf7840c83d80702fd6feb2fee4b00f80199bc37c484d","at":"2026-08-08T19:12:50.467Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-11-{"id":"cor-perfect-normality-is-hereditary","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 1.2 uses that perfect normality makes every ambient closed set C a countable intersection of open sets, but cites only F1, which gives subspace closed traces and the definition of G-delta. No listed fact licenses that move.","context_sha256":"761cd09c4f4cec79854524c9d167c413806e3d4adbf9a48219937eebdee07684","item_sha256":"56b6388cdc7f12277e6b7701a5e03cf17bebb808bfc92d7441be61e2cb62b07b","at":"2026-08-08T19:12:50.535Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-12-{"id":"ex-cauchy-complete-not-complete-field","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified each fact against its cited result and the sequence estimates correctly establish the listed completeness properties and the explicit Cauchy limit.","context_sha256":"032ade782f591626bac9ca097d8015533c05f71aa823613609d1abacdaf666a7","item_sha256":"7ee813d301a9e4aa07fc31be62bac9af02fbec5470e29367fe3029451a9e4729","at":"2026-08-08T19:12:50.948Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-13-{"id":"ex-a-urysohn-function-on-the-real-line","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 1.1 cites only real-valued continuity of max and min. It never establishes that this real continuity gives continuity of g as a map from R to the subspace [0,1], which is the continuity required by Urysohn's lemma.","context_sha256":"eff9e468b8377b3dfc18290617526185377093760e8c8b1899f79b86f3b5e07e","item_sha256":"6b14257753d55d5189e61136d8d218a3e3ddef9190c01ae2147472f913fc12d4","at":"2026-08-08T19:12:51.167Z"}
