research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-48-{"id":"def-gauge-of-pseudometrics","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":false,"reason":"The definition asserts without justification that the family is a filter base and that the generated filter is a uniformity; the citations do not license these claims.","context_sha256":"c10e9323395214d6508cdb73daf19a2cd4382f1d0f4d22c208c8a1b621041469","item_sha256":"3e786bab30b61294ab7f87c86a3e0458e6e767b2ed7fed340edabeb9e85e1a22","at":"2026-08-08T19:15:23.446Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-49-{"id":"lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":false,"reason":"A1 omits the requirement that entourages contain the diagonal. Steps 2.1 and 2.2 use this unlisted property while citing only A1, making the proof unjustified.","context_sha256":"83126cc7f9183525d94f78eda97ff3c690b905f8ef47868805b56aa09dcd3825","item_sha256":"fc16c6eafa9286126192ca3e11f839a7e746ba42968661cef7db5811ae47d433","at":"2026-08-08T19:15:23.868Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-50-{"id":"thm-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-unique-compatible-uniformity","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"L1 misstates its citation: the cited theorem makes all covers admitting an open refinement into the uniform-cover structure, not merely the open covers. The open covers alone are not closed under arbitrary coarsening, so need not form a uniform-cover structure.","context_sha256":"fb1e7a24f86561d80f3c1a95996e541cbc1ff0bf25c904f805c2499901d07262","item_sha256":"bfa50a1693d8ae18cef5a87913de5e6cce3d3bf681f215c07c568b2b8e27b17b","at":"2026-08-08T19:15:24.841Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-51-{"id":"thm-compact-hausdorff-open-cover-uniformity","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the closure and star-refinement axioms and both inclusions establishing that the recovered uniform topology is the original topology.","context_sha256":"d407e17ed410500f1827a7d5bb34c8d8d9564a16678619957547eb8963d75b03","item_sha256":"9714c286f45c7a29239b93238a87f0f93761b6347bc61b166b0a20fd7a578548","at":"2026-08-08T19:15:26.801Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl:52:{"id":"ex-harmonic-series-diverges","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"All steps are correctly justified by the cited facts; the condensation and block arguments are logically sound, and the explicit bound is correctly derived.","context_sha256":"0153498dd3e71524d06e01e588223f1d43294cb2875b60c627fc75efa4163788","item_sha256":"dfaa02b7731703fcb77aeb621a75b2d99e1a764376dff1335f9f9eecb42d6e9d","at":"2026-08-08T19:15:35.100Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-53-{"id":"thm-composition-of-function-limits","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"[L4] is not a fact: it merely says \"Limit point, and neighbourhoods\" rather than stating either cited definition. This violates the required citation fidelity and gives no checkable proposition for step 3.1.","context_sha256":"60f2625f688f45c6d441a0c0ea894265ae39e5a783badf667e530f6ac118e4f2","item_sha256":"9fe976c82eb9b2b96b67d18bf8fc5bd3caa1876700f744c921e5fef6a095fdf0","at":"2026-08-08T19:15:48.558Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-54-{"id":"thm-countably-based-uniformity-is-pseudometrizable","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 1.1 applies L2 without establishing its required condition E_0=X times X. L1 supplies only a decreasing symmetric base with triple-composite control. Reindexing after adjoining X times X would fix this, but the proof does not do it.","context_sha256":"b6c2345d8831af1f76dabb2c75f52b4559701f1bf39ab97f8a04893cd450e36d","item_sha256":"ff1e5d289f56dc089165657c41a93acde9a219452d18a667cba75161b91989ca","at":"2026-08-08T19:15:51.496Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-55-{"id":"lem-convergent-filters-are-cauchy","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"Proof correctly derives Cauchy property from convergence using symmetric entourage square root and neighbourhood base; all steps properly cite faithful facts.","context_sha256":"540e55b8b694b2794ca283bfed0d33e052c457c633db624c833a17141a1d03e2","item_sha256":"ca69cb65055da2fd3b32a37d91019f1a5b3ced7924506a594115785e00846b88","at":"2026-08-08T19:15:55.079Z"}
research/audit/wave7-judge.jsonl-56-{"id":"thm-complete-and-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-compact","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"Each step follows directly from the cited facts: L1 gives Cauchy, L2 gives convergence, L3 gives compactness under the ultrafilter lemma assumption.","context_sha256":"8c92a2ac58082f34636d55fe0c65e40edc2127f0e9e485611c7086cb86e4cbf9","item_sha256":"d4fac0358df324f6c1cef51dafc5693327aac1e2384173d118a827d34e28739f","at":"2026-08-08T19:15:59.043Z"}
