research/audit/wave7-judge-adjudications.jsonl:4:{"id":"ex-harmonic-series-diverges","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"0153498dd3e71524d06e01e588223f1d43294cb2875b60c627fc75efa4163788","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","defect_type":"other","item_sha256":"460e60ed223398384e44117b0be84d044ba07ff9249cd65d0d41ed23ae031d89","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-08T19:32:01Z","note":"Terra is correct. The introduction says verbatim that the bound gives 'the slowest divergence any explicit series on this page exhibits', while ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series explicitly displays $1/(kH_k)$ and says it 'diverges more slowly still.' This is a false public comparison claim, not an omitted proof step, and licenses deletion of the exclusivity claim."}
